Subject: [PATCH 1/3] C20, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M31;
 register row P-310): B335'S SENTENCE THAT ANY MASS IS EXACTLY DEGENERATE IS
 SHARPENED BY A DATED NOTE, AS ITS READER FOUND

The card is relays/cards/cld-advisor_C20_three-record-keeping-debts-of-the-register.md, committed before the work.

P-310. B335 says that the generation Z/3 is a deck transformation and an isometry, "so every real geometric invariant
(and any mass) is exactly degenerate". The register's row records its reader's finding (L237's reader, in the
parked-items sweep): this overstates, because B325 and a 3x3 circulant check split the masses. B325's own verdict line,
banked before B335, refuted the claimed Z/3-protection of the two light eigenvalues (distinct 1-dim irreps that a
Z/3-invariant cubic can split).

A dated note on B335's page, after the sentence, and at the end of its verdict line, quoting the row and B325; a
sharpening, not a retraction (the row's word): the verdict, the isometry and the values the page confirms are unchanged.
The circulant check is the reader's, recorded in the row; it is not computed again here, and no mathematics in the note
is the builder's.

THE LOCK, tests/test_c20_record_keeping.py (C20's three rows will share it): the note stands after the old words and
quotes the row, B325's verdict line and B335's own sentence, each found in its source; the verdict line carries its
note; planted, the note taken out, the note moved above the old words, the verdict line's note taken out, each reported
alone. B335's own lock passes. The early record index, which shows each early arc's verdict line, carries the note,
written again by its script. BEFORE: on the tree before this patch the new test fails.

